  "schema_version": "space_overview_v1",
  "sections": [
    {
      "body": "This scope frames mind as a problem of integration, selection, and trainable regulation. Tononi defines consciousness through differentiated yet unified information integration, while the mindfulness records caution that mindfulness is an umbrella term spanning heterogeneous faculties, practices, interventions, and measures. The attention evidence adds a more operational layer: the Attention Network Test separates alerting, orienting, and conflict monitoring, and alpha-band work treats suppression of irrelevant input as an active attentional mechanism. S-ART then bridges these strands by modeling mindfulness as multidimensional mental training aimed at self-awareness, self-regulation, and self-transcendence rather than as a single capacity.",
