      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "Several themes recur across the evidence. First, conscious access is described as depending on integrated organization: high-\u03a6 complexes, thalamocortical specialization plus integration, and reduced consciousness when integration is anatomically or functionally disrupted. Second, attention is treated as separable subsystems and as sensory gating: mindfulness training is reported to affect orienting, alerting, and conflict monitoring differently, while alpha power is linked to suppressing distracting regions and lowering visual excitability. Third, mindfulness is treated by S-ART as a coordinated set of mechanisms including attention regulation, emotion regulation, extinction and reconsolidation, prosociality, non-attachment, and decentering. Fourth, clinical and public claims are constrained by construct ambiguity, mixed efficacy, undermeasured adverse effects, and the need for more precise intervention descriptions.",
