      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "The records mostly agree on decomposition: consciousness, attention, self-processing, and mindfulness outcomes are all presented as structured phenomena whose mechanisms should not be collapsed into a single global score. Relations reinforce this pattern by connecting ambiguous mindfulness definitions to weak self-report validity, intervention heterogeneity to mixed efficacy, and S-ART component research needs to mindfulness as a multidimensional skillset. The main tension is not a direct contradiction but a difference in evidential posture. Mechanistic and framework papers propose plausible routes from meditation to attention, physiology, and self-processing change, while the critical mindfulness review warns that hype, immature trials, weak measures, preliminary neuroimaging, and undermeasured adverse events make broad benefit claims unsafe.",
