      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "The evidence mix is methodologically varied. Tononi supplies a formal theory with \u03a6, complexes, and qualia-space relationships, applying those constructs to thalamocortical organization and disconnection. Jha, Krompinger, and Baime provide behavioral ANT evidence, but their own claim set flags small groups, no active-training control, behavioral measures only, and imperfect protocol control. Foxe and Snyder synthesize electrophysiological, cuing, sensory, and causal/predictive evidence for alpha as active suppression. Van Dam and colleagues audit the field\u2019s construct definitions, questionnaires, clinical designs, neuroimaging interpretations, and adverse-event practices. S-ART is a neurobiological framework review that organizes hypothesized mechanisms and explicitly calls for longitudinal component measurement, dose tracking, practice-quality assessment, and adverse-effect monitoring.",
