        "source-04-mind-the-hype-a-critical-evaluation-and-prescriptive-agenda-for-research-on-mind-w2761197918--79c0d54db997",
        "source-05-self-awareness-self-regulation-and-self-transcendence-s-art-a-framework-for-unde-w2005022581--615ee4e1923f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "The scope leaves several questions open. The consciousness material needs empirical bridges between \u03a6-based formal claims and practical measurement across biological and artificial systems. The attention material needs larger and better controlled tests that separate training history, task repetition, and active control effects. Alpha suppression remains a strong organizing hypothesis, but the balance of cortico-cortical and thalamo-cortical control needs sharper specification. Mindfulness research needs shared terminology, construct-valid measures, preregistered replications, detailed protocol reporting, active adverse-event assessment, and condition-specific clinical claims. S-ART adds the need to track dose, practice quality, component mechanisms, and possible harms over time rather than inferring a single mindfulness effect.",
